WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Do you
have Windows workloads

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.150
that need modernization?

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.010
Keep watching as
we cover how you

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.600
can use Anthos to modernize and
run your Windows applications.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.988
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.740
Hi, I'm Priyanka Vergadia,
and welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.410
With Anthos, our goal
is to make it seamless

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.840
for you to modernize and
manage your workloads

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.880
in the environments
that you prefer,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.340
whether it is on-prem,
Google Cloud, Edge,

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.840
or a different cloud.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.360
With about 50% of the
enterprise workloads

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.180
running on Windows servers,
it's important to see

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.660
how Windows workloads can take
advantage of the modernization

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:40.030
benefits that Anthos offers.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.890
Up until recently,
Kubernetes was

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.170
limited to Linux-based
applications,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.750
preventing enterprise
applications running on Windows

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.110
servers from taking advantage
of the benefits of agility,

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.860
speed of development, and
simplified management.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.250
Last year, 2019, the
open source community

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.920
brought Windows servers
container support

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.170
in Kubernetes 1.14.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.239
Building on the
OSS functionality,

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:07.340
Anthos has added several
out of the box security,

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.600
scalability, integration,
and management capabilities,

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.240
through features like private
cluster support, shielded VMs,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.280
and regional clusters and
industry-first full weight auto

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.580
scaling available
only in Anthos GKE.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.570
By running Windows Server apps
as containers on Anthos GKE,

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.930
you can reduce the licensing
burden and vendor dependencies

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.990
along with many of the benefits
that Linux applications

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.120
have enjoyed for years.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.040
With the general
availability of Windows

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.220
on Anthos on Google Cloud,
you can run your Windows

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.620
and Linux-based
workloads side by side

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.220
with the master or control plane
and the node pools attached

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.030
to it.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:50.470
You can run the SAC semi-annual
channel version or the LTSC,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.860
the long-term servicing channel
version of the Windows Server

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.140
in the Windows node pools.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.980
Kubelet and kube-proxy run
natively on the Windows nodes,

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.190
allowing you to run mixed
Windows and Linux container

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.630
workloads in the same cluster.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.470
Now, whether you're modernizing
an existing Windows app

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.590
or creating a new one, the
first thing that you need to do

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.670
is to create a cluster to
deploy your Windows-based app.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.910
To do that in the Anthos
UI, create the cluster,

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.730
provide a name
and add node pool.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.480
Create a node and select
Windows semi-annual or long term

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.450
service channel as
the image, and create.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.130
Once you have the
cluster created,

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.340
you can deploy a new Windows
application in the cluster

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.620
or migrate an
existing Windows app.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.670
To migrate an
existing application,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.260
you could use Migrate for
Anthos V2K for Windows.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.860
The solution migrates IAS
web applications, ASP.net,

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.220
and Windows Server apps
from VMs to Windows Server

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.130
2019 containers on Anthos GKE.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.710
It automatically extracts
application files

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.410
and configurations
from Compute Engine VMs

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.140
and creates a suggested
migration plan.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.910
This is an auto-generated
plan, but you

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.950
can customize it if you need.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.310
It generates artifacts like
a ZIP file with application

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:10.430
contents and settings and a
Docker file with the recipe

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:12.800
to build the deployable image.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.470
The Docker file is then
used to build an image

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:18.470
and then validate
the generated image.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.260
We understand that modernizing
your applications entail

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.090
more than just deploying
and managing containers.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.630
This is why we're working
with several partners

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.640
to build a strong ecosystem.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.430
We're excited to announce that
these partners have already

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.040
worked to integrate their
solutions with Windows

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.020
on Anthos GKE.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.660
Migrate for Anthos provides
a fast and simple way

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:42.080
to move existing workloads
to modernized orchestration

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.260
and application management
without requiring access

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.160
to source code, rewriting, or
re-architecting applications.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.400
We are committed to helping you
in your modernization journey,

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.350
regardless of the
type of platform

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.500
or workloads you use,
Linux or Windows.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.650
Soon, Windows on Anthos will
be available on premises

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.360
and on other clouds.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.130
To learn more, check out the
documentation linked below.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.800
And for more Anthos
content, don't

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.830
forget to subscribe and follow
the Anthos 101 playlist.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

